Sure, here's the full configuration. You just need to add it in your OpenCode config file.
**Config file locations:**

| OS | Path |
|---|---|
| macOS / Linux | `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` |
| Windows | `%USERPROFILE%\.config\opencode\opencode.json` |

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  // ... your other configs
  "provider": {
    "bailian-payg": {
      "models": {
        "qwen3.7-max": {
          "name": "Qwen3.7 Max",
          "reasoning": true,
          "variants": {
            "low": { "thinking": { "budgetTokens": 4096, "type": "enabled" } },
            "medium": { "thinking": { "budgetTokens": 8192, "type": "enabled" } },
            "high": { "thinking": { "budgetTokens": 16384, "type": "enabled" } },
            "max": { "thinking": { "budgetTokens": 32768, "type": "enabled" } }
          }
        }
      },
      "name": "Alibaba Cloud Model Studio",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/anthropic",
      "options": {
        "apiKey": "your-apiKey",
        "baseURL": "https://{WorkspaceId}.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/apps/anthropic/v1",
        "setCacheKey": true
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Don't forget to replace `"your-apiKey"` and `"baseURL"` with your actual API key and baseURL before saving. The baseURL and API format might differ in different regions.
For more details, see the [OpenCode Config Docs](https://opencode.ai/docs/config/).
